 `class ChatV2 extends ChatV3` ([`../v3/`](../v3/readme.md), step 2 of [views-on-messages.md](/framework/core/Session/Chat/doc/views-on-messages.md)). Everything is ChatV3: it draws `session.messages` (a card per Prompt, in the chat list's own order, with the Replies that answer it found by `re.to`), the live draft, pause-based paragraphs, "show raw". V2 adds only three things:
 
-- **The ✓/🧠 marks**, beside the title of the newest Prompt only. ✓ colours once the fast seat has the line; 🧠 colours once an answer actually exists (a Reply after the smart seat's receipt, or the Prompt's own title/text). They still read the Prompt TASK's `sent.fast`/`sent.smart` (`Sessions.mark_sent`), not a field on the message — step 3 of the plan moves them there. Until then, `ChatV2.js` keeps a small tracker (`prompt_of`, `sent_by_task`) over the V1 `{chat}`/`{sent}` broadcast lines ChatV3 skips, the one piece of the old `ChatV2Model` this step still needs.
+- **The ✓/🧠 marks**, beside the title of the newest Prompt only. ✓ colours once the fast seat has the line; 🧠 colours once an answer actually exists (a Reply after the smart seat's receipt, or the Prompt's own title/text). Step 3 of the plan: they now read `p.sent` (`{fast?: {at}, smart?: {at}}`) straight off the Prompt message — `Sessions.mark_sent` writes it there (`ChatWriter.sent_line`), so the V1 `{chat}`/`{sent}` broadcast-line tracker is gone. A session recorded before step 3 has no `sent` on its messages, so its newest Prompt shows no marks; only sessions written after the switch do.
 - **A Reply beside the sentence it answers**, while a Prompt has no refined text yet (dictation mode): `ChatV2.js` overrides two small hooks ChatV3 exposes for this (`paragraph()`, `trailing_replies()`) to draw one row per sentence, with the Reply whose `re.to` names it drawn right beside, instead of in the trailing list below the whole card. Once a Prompt gets refined text, replies go back to the normal trailing list, same as plain ChatV3. "Show raw" (ChatV3's own feature, shown when `Prompt.clean` has entries) stays ChatV3's: V2 adds nothing to it this step — a raw-toggled, already-refined Prompt still lists its replies in the trailing list, not beside the raw lines (see Decisions).
 - **Its own CSS** (`ChatV2.css`): the marks and the beside-sentence layout only; everything else is `../v3/ChatV3.css`'s own rules. `ChatV2.read()` adds the `chat-v3` class to `$box` itself, so every caller (this demo, the session page's Chat tab, the drawer/✦ sheet) gets ChatV3's column width and phone padding for free, with no change needed at the call site.
 
-Try it: [/framework/ext/Chat/v2/](/framework/ext/Chat/v2/) draws [fixture/messages-session.jsonl](fixture/messages-session.jsonl) (V3's own fixture, plus a few `{chat}`/`{sent}` lines so the marks have data); `?src=<url of any session.jsonl>` draws that session, live. Shot with both the marks and the live draft visible: [shots/chat-v2-marks-and-live-draft.png](/framework/ai/sessions/2026/10/20/session-e00f55c9/dictation-v3/v2-subclass/shots/chat-v2-marks-and-live-draft.png).
+Try it: [/framework/ext/Chat/v2/](/framework/ext/Chat/v2/) draws [fixture/messages-session.jsonl](fixture/messages-session.jsonl) (V3's own fixture, plus a few `sent` lines on two of its Prompt messages so the marks have data); `?src=<url of any session.jsonl>` draws that session, live. Shot with both the marks and the live draft visible: [shots/chat-v2-marks-and-live-draft.png](/framework/ai/sessions/2026/10/20/session-e00f55c9/dictation-v3/v2-subclass/shots/chat-v2-marks-and-live-draft.png).
 
